                "reply_count": 3,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Medicaid, or what we in Massachusetts call MassHealth, plays a critical role in our communities:\n\n\u2695\ufe0f More than 2 million residents rely on Medicaid for health coverage\n\ud83d\udcb0 Medicaid brings in $13 billion each year \u2013 half of all federal funding for Massachusetts\n\ud83e\uddd1\u200d\u2695\ufe0f Medicaid directly supports 125,000 health care jobs\n\ud83c\udfe5 Medicaid provides one-fifth of revenue for hospitals and half the revenue for nursing facilities and community health centers\n\nIn my district, EVERY hospital has a public payer mix that accounts for more than two-thirds of revenue. \n\nWhether a hospital closes or has to make significant cuts, the proposed Medicaid cuts under the GOP tax scam will have devastating consequences for patients, health care workers, and entire communities.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
